// Raiders. The sprite program, MACHINES A, build 7: MACHINE WRECKS. Every machine that died left the same flat turning oval as
// every other, sized by its radius: a Sentry, a Crawler and a Warden all died as the same blob. Now a dead machine leaves its
// own body for the length of the death animation: drawn by its own painter with its eye gone black, darkened to under half its
// brightness, settling a few units into the ground and tipping over a little, then fading out over the oval and the burst it
// always left. A Crier drops out of the air. The body is painted into one small shared scratch canvas (SPRWRECK) with the same
// camera, darkened there and stamped back. Drawn only: nothing in the fight reads it, no random numbers.
var SPRWRECK=null, SPRWRECKK={sentry:1,crawler:1,snitch:1,listener:1,warden:1,choir:1,howler:1,bulwark:1};
